{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pulls/1205","id":5209104168,"node_id":"PR_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABNnyfKA","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pull/1205","diff_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pull/1205.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pull/1205.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1205","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pulls/1205/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pulls/1205/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1205/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/statuses/21061aa532401398db70c59a596debf330f70744","number":1205,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add guarded campaign curation and canonical publication operators","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The ten-worker unmatched-ingredient campaign needs guarded source application and canonical publication for an explicitly reviewed multi-owner plan. These operators bind frozen source cases, published proposals, independent acceptance, producer bytes and complete owner inventories before writing, then preserve recoverable receipts and native publication lineage.\n\nDepends on #1158 at `e000d66dd26ab053e9b17ce7bf8d3c873c3dde99`; the base is that dependency branch. This PR contains implementation, regression tests and review evidence. Campaign ingredient edits and release products will be a separate dependent PR after final scientific and plan acceptance.\n\nCurrent code head: `21061aa532401398db70c59a596debf330f70744`. Exact-head independent re-review and final validation are in progress. No maintained campaign ingredient application or merge has occurred.\n\n- Source application uses guarded writers, genuine preimages, closed proposal/acceptance bindings, complete inventories and exclusive receipts. Promotions preserve their actual unmapped origins.\n- Canonical publication binds actual native generation, sidecars, policy history, projected alias checks and native receipts. Historical attribution stays historical; changing an owner does not confer scientific approval.\n- #1251 preserves inherited collision families while refusing new collision pairs. #1252 permits bounded rejected-record maintenance and genuine UNMAPPED-to-REJECTED retirement while retaining identity, name, path and history checks.\n- #741's explicit demotion route requires an independently accepted exact relocation tuple, genuine published origins and no prior owner chain on either path. MAPPED-to-AMBIGUOUS demotion removes ontology grounding; publication requires zero generated ontology/registry rows and removes every old subject slot. It does not decide Angustmycin A/C identity.\n- #1255 parses literal NUL-delimited Git paths, including authentic Unicode owner filenames. #1256 rechecks the accepted baseline HEAD and tracked-file scope throughout live source application and checks that same HEAD throughout live publication. Unrelated changes already present are refused before writing. Historical completed verification still permits later commits when the exact content and proof remain valid.\n\nAddresses #1174, #1194, #1195, #1197, #1198, #1200, #1214, #1251, #1252, #1255 and #1256, plus the bounded #741 workflow prerequisite. Earlier adversarial findings, failed probes and superseded reviews remain preserved. The existing archives under `reports/unmatched_campaign_operators_1174_20261108/independent-review/` and `issue1214/` retain their identities. The [earlier review receipt](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pull/1205#issuecomment-6718353021) applies only to its stated head.\n\nValidation checkpoint:\n\n- The source #1256 author run passed 441 source/publication/native integration cases using the corrected source and previous publisher. The separate publisher run passed 157 cases against both corrected operators, including 15 actual pinned-Claw integration cases, with zero skips. These overlapping runs are not summed or presented as final independent approval. Ruff, Black and Mypy passed on the respective corrected files.\n- The original 16c source-test prefix is byte-identical. Two #1255 negative harnesses now require the stronger early refusal with unchanged owners and no output receipt. Existing publisher assertions remain, with genuine Git fixture baselines and a private native lock workspace. No test is removed or skipped, and no gate, workflow, threshold or pin is changed.\n- Whole `just qc` and `just test` passed at predecessor16c: 5,654 passed, 116 existing skips, 31 warnings and zero failures; all nine real native integration cases ran. Its inputs remained unchanged. Final21061 validation is starting; the predecessor results do not substitute for final-head checks. Rule B4's absent default ontology path was reported explicitly rather than claimed as complete label verification.\n- Worker08's separate review of exact16c found #1255 and #1256; it remains `needs_curation`. Its 337 distinct passes came from 328 initial passes plus a later nine-case native rerun; initial lock failures are retained. A new independent technical and skeptical review is running on exact21061.\n- Actual native cases use isolated Claw `76c1ebeea3fc7f80bf1abe044688f298f390cfac` and the immutable eac469f1 fixture with all 27 historical receipts. Explicit external roots are required; CI may skip those optional integration cases where the roots are unavailable. Local execution remains separately evidenced.\n\nCurrent author manifests under `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/integration/`: `late-head1256-fix-v1/MANIFEST.json` (`27f1ace688079339e5698e20ef7354b7553ce52bd043caa2daa62101d6f1180a`) and `publisher-late-head1256-fix-v1/portable/MANIFEST.json` (`2426579669e0c4de717192751c3d03326f497c3cca0f8f4542f33969b980a920`). The coordinator verified all 31 and 85 declared members before the ordinary commit and push. Final reviewed evidence will be archived with explicit scope. This PR grants no source-case, owner, role or supported-export approval.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-08T06:01:35Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T12:08:48Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"6f42aa79f5cd7bb36fb42804216e8525e3c4a408","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"CultureBotAI:curate/all-unmatched-source-integration-20261107","ref":"curate/all-unmatched-source-integration-20261107","repo":{"id":1175495445,"node_id":"R_kgDORhCjFQ","name":"MediaIngredientMech","full_name":"CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","owner":{"login":"CultureBotAI","id":233210009,"node_id":"O_kgDODeaAmQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/233210009?v=